1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,240
This series was created
for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:02,240 --> 00:00:05,680
The characters, actions, locations,
dialogue, languages, ceremonies,

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:08,120
and artistic elements depicted in this series

4
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,040
are fictional and based on imagination,

5
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:13,920
incorporating the beauty
of the region's diverse cultures,

6
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:18,400
including those
of Lanna, Myanmar, the Tai peoples, and China.

7
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,560
It is not intended to disrespect any history,

8
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,600
ethnic group, organization, profession,
or group of individuals.

9
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:26,040
Viewer discretion is advised.

10
00:00:26,040 --> 00:00:27,880
[Previously]
<i>The King has issued a royal decree</i>

11
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,800
<i>appointing Lady Fongnuan</i>

12
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:33,040
<i>as a lady-in-waiting in the outer court
of Wiang Kaew.</i>

13
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:36,080
<i>It was me, Homjan.
I had you summoned to Wiang Kaew.</i>

14
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,920
<i>I wish to know everything about
Maneethip, especially her past.</i>

15
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,560
<i>Is something wrong?</i>

16
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:45,240
<i>I'll order the soldiers
to bring the bandits' bodies back to Ullavee.</i>

17
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:48,440
<i>I want to investigate and find out
who was behind this.</i>

18
00:00:48,440 --> 00:00:50,040
<i>Take the bodies away for cremation.</i>

19
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:51,800
<i>I don't know anything about court duties.</i>

20
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:53,240
<i>I'll teach you.</i>

21
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:56,640
<i>Come here tomorrow to begin your training.</i>

22
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,480
<i>Tomorrow?</i>

23
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,720
<i>Yes.</i>

24
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,280
- Add a little more firewood.
- Yes, Your Highness.

25
00:01:16,240 --> 00:01:18,880
You never seem to learn.

26
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:23,600
You must be careful when wrapping Miang.
It's not something you can rush.

27
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:42,040
Wrap the Miang tightly
so the filling doesn't fall out.

28
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:43,880
Yes, Your Highness.

29
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:08,680
Your Highness! Blood! Blood!

30
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:10,920
- Blood!
- Your Highness!

31
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:13,280
Are you hurt?

32
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:14,960
- Blood!
- Your Highness!

33
00:02:15,880 --> 00:02:18,120
- Your Highness!
- Your Highness!

34
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:21,560
- Blood!
- You're bleeding, Your Highness!

35
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,800
- Blood! Your Highness!
- Blood! Your Highness!

36
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:26,840
Blood! Your Highness!

37
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,680
Your Highness!

38
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:33,280
Your Highness!

39
00:02:46,720 --> 00:02:48,080
Your Highness.

40
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:54,160
- Your Highness! Your Highness! Your Highness!
- Your Highness! Your Highness! Your Highness!

41
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,840
I'm sorry.

42
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:07,840
I couldn't protect you or our child.

43
00:03:53,120 --> 00:03:55,360
Forgive me, Your Majesty.

44
00:03:57,120 --> 00:04:00,320
But I no longer wish to be a royal consort.

45
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:05,960
Please let me live
as an ordinary lady-in-waiting...

46
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:09,240
and serve you here in Wiang Kaew.

47
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:21,600
If that is what you wish,

48
00:04:22,840 --> 00:04:24,480
so be it.

49
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:31,640
I shall appoint you Head Lady-in-Waiting,

50
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:35,680
to oversee all the ladies-in-waiting...

51
00:04:36,760 --> 00:04:39,680
in both the Outer and Inner Courts.

52
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:47,240
But you must stay by my side...

53
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:50,080
for the rest of your life.

54
00:05:01,520 --> 00:05:05,000
Whoever poisoned my child...

55
00:05:06,440 --> 00:05:10,040
will suffer a terrible fate.

56
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:18,720
[Irresistible Feelings]

57
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:20,960
When speaking to the King,

58
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:23,600
use the proper pronoun for yourself.

59
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:29,120
The same applies when speaking to royals
of either the Outer or Inner Court.

60
00:07:30,040 --> 00:07:31,680
Do you understand?

61
00:07:32,440 --> 00:07:34,160
Yes, my lady!

62
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:40,480
Lower your voice. Don't sound so commanding.

63
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,800
You're not a soldier.

64
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:45,080
And don't show your teeth when you smile.

65
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:47,760
It's improper.

66
00:07:48,720 --> 00:07:51,520
- Yes, my lady.
- Too slow.

67
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:53,840
- Answer at the right pace.
- Yes, my lady.

68
00:07:56,680 --> 00:08:01,800
In the King's presence,
sit properly and avoid looking directly at him.

69
00:08:01,800 --> 00:08:04,480
Keep your eyes on the floor,
three cubits ahead of you.

70
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:07,800
Keep your hands folded in front of you,
where the King can see them.

71
00:08:07,800 --> 00:08:10,000
Three cubits?

72
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,120
How am I supposed to see anything?

73
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:31,360
This is how you must sit. Remember it.

74
00:08:31,360 --> 00:08:33,200
Yes, my lady.

75
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:37,640
When presenting something to the King,
you must move only forward or backward.

76
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:41,640
Never turn your back on him.
Don't stomp your feet.

77
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:46,320
Keep your steps light and measured.
Neither too fast nor too slow.

78
00:08:49,440 --> 00:08:52,440
Too fast. Start again.

79
00:09:02,560 --> 00:09:04,080
Too slow.

80
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,560
Start again.

81
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,040
Then how fast am I supposed to walk, my lady?

82
00:09:38,160 --> 00:09:39,520
Oops!

83
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,320
Goodness gracious!

84
00:09:44,560 --> 00:09:45,880
Start again.

85
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:09,760
Did I pass, my lady?

86
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,120
Try again.

87
00:10:58,000 --> 00:10:59,640
You are all dismissed.

88
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:09,880
I found rice from Ullavee
in Merng Mang's granary.

89
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:22,680
All rice looks alike.

90
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:28,040
I've tasted rice from Ullavee and Merng Mang.

91
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:30,920
I can tell the difference
even with my eyes closed.

92
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:35,920
If you won't confess,

93
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:41,400
I'll tell the King
that the four thieves you had cremated...

94
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:44,800
were actually your own soldiers.

95
00:11:45,800 --> 00:11:51,720
You staged the whole theft
to steal rice from Ullavee.

96
00:11:55,240 --> 00:11:59,840
You've got nothing but a sack of rice,
and you dare accuse me?

97
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:05,160
How convenient. What a shameless lie!
How could those thieves have been my soldiers?

98
00:12:05,160 --> 00:12:08,040
Their bodies bore the tattoos
of Merng Mang soldiers.

99
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:14,040
I doubt your soldiers would be pleased
to learn you killed your own men.

100
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:16,480
Just to cover up your lies.

101
00:12:16,480 --> 00:12:18,800
Confess now,

102
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:24,720
or I'll bring your soldiers before the King
and expose the truth.

103
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:26,160
Your choice!

104
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,000
I...

105
00:12:32,080 --> 00:12:33,880
choose to silence you!

106
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:43,280
You're on Merng Mang soil.
You think you can threaten me here?

107
00:12:43,920 --> 00:12:45,520
I'm not threatening you.

108
00:12:52,800 --> 00:12:55,320
I know you've been exiled.

109
00:12:55,920 --> 00:12:58,920
You need somewhere to stay.

110
00:12:58,920 --> 00:13:01,240
Why not join me?

111
00:13:01,240 --> 00:13:03,760
I'll make sure you're well looked after,
Mueang Fah.

112
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:05,760
I have no intention of staying in Merng Mang!

113
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:12,480
I won't mention the rice,

114
00:13:12,480 --> 00:13:15,240
the soldiers' bodies, or the fake bandits.

115
00:13:16,040 --> 00:13:21,000
But you must tell Indraraja
exactly what I instruct you to say.

116
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:31,200
You should send Mueang Fah
to serve in the King's Guard at Wiang Kaew.

117
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:34,160
Why?

118
00:13:34,160 --> 00:13:36,280
I've heard...

119
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:40,960
more people are growing suspicious
of our extortion of caravan merchants.

120
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:46,000
If we put Mueang Fah in Wiang Kaew
as our eyes and ears,

121
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:51,680
he can keep us informed
and keep the King in the dark.

122
00:13:53,080 --> 00:13:55,480
I see your point,

123
00:13:55,480 --> 00:13:57,960
but Mueang Fah was born
during the Hour of the Plunderer.

124
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,400
He is destined to bring disaster
upon the kingdom.

125
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:03,480
Father would never allow him
to live in Wiang Kaew.

126
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,640
I have a plan.

127
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,840
You have all come here today.

128
00:14:45,840 --> 00:14:47,760
What brings you here?

129
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:56,440
The drought has driven bandits
to raid the borderlands for rice.

130
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:59,520
They may even dare to raid the Royal Granary.

131
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:03,840
I fear for your safety, Father.

132
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:08,120
I therefore ask you to issue a royal decree...

133
00:15:09,080 --> 00:15:13,120
appointing Mueang Fah
to the King's Guard at Wiang Kaew.

134
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,080
Why must it be Mueang Fah?

135
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:19,360
Mueang Fah is a skilled fighter.
Everyone knows that.

136
00:15:19,360 --> 00:15:23,960
He has fought bandits along the borders.
He knows all their tricks.

137
00:15:23,960 --> 00:15:25,800
With him here,

138
00:15:25,800 --> 00:15:30,520
I'm certain he can protect
both you and Wiang Kaew.

139
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:38,880
Rest assured, Your Majesty.

140
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:43,080
Prince Mueang Fah is a formidable warrior.

141
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:48,480
He has fought countless bandits
along the borders.

142
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:50,720
With him protecting Your Majesty,

143
00:15:50,720 --> 00:15:55,360
Wiang Kaew will be much safer.

144
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:59,320
But what about the prophecy?

145
00:16:04,600 --> 00:16:08,080
I've studied Ullavee's fortunes
for this period.

146
00:16:08,080 --> 00:16:13,200
Our kingdom remains strong, Your Majesty.

147
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:18,600
Prince Mueang Fah's fate
poses no danger to Ullavee.

148
00:16:27,480 --> 00:16:29,080
Father,

149
00:16:30,760 --> 00:16:35,280
I allowed Mueang Fah
to stay in Ullavee some time ago.

150
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:38,560
Nothing troubling has happened since.

151
00:16:38,560 --> 00:16:44,520
Perhaps his hour of birth
has no effect on Ullavee after all.

152
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,520
If you all insist,

153
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:54,080
I shall grant your request.

154
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:58,000
Mueang Fah may come to Wiang Kaew.

155
00:16:58,920 --> 00:17:04,840
But once the bandits are dealt with,
he must return to Merng Mang, the border city.

156
00:17:14,760 --> 00:17:16,920
I did as you asked.

157
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:18,640
Now keep your end of the bargain.

158
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:21,720
I'm a man of my word.

159
00:17:21,720 --> 00:17:23,560
I keep my promises.

160
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:27,400
If you tell anyone,

161
00:17:27,400 --> 00:17:32,320
I'll have a grave dug for you
deep in the forests of Merng Mang.

162
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:36,000
You'll never live to return to Ullavee.

163
00:17:58,720 --> 00:18:02,880
In Wiang Kaew,
there are two groups of ladies-in-waiting.

164
00:18:04,240 --> 00:18:05,880
Outer Court ladies-in-waiting...

165
00:18:05,880 --> 00:18:10,160
attend to the Royal Palace,
Royal Residence, Royal Library,

166
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:13,080
and the residences of male royals.

167
00:18:13,080 --> 00:18:16,120
Inner Court ladies-in-waiting
attend to the Royal Kitchen,

168
00:18:16,120 --> 00:18:22,240
the Herb Room, the Fragrance Room,
and the residences of female royals.

169
00:18:22,240 --> 00:18:25,920
All ladies-in-waiting are under my supervision.

170
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:31,240
All ladies-in-waiting must perform their duties
from dawn until dusk.

171
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:37,200
You must rise before sunrise
and carry out all your duties.

172
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:43,440
From now on, you must watch your every move.

173
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:46,960
Mind your manners,
your words, and your gestures.

174
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:50,120
Remember everything I've taught you.

175
00:18:50,120 --> 00:18:54,880
There is one rule
more important than serving the King himself.

176
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:02,680
Never reveal the Royal Residence's secrets.

177
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:04,960
Do not wander about at night.

178
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:09,520
Do not pry into anything you overhear.

179
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:11,480
Do you understand?

180
00:19:11,480 --> 00:19:13,520
Yes, my lady.

181
00:19:13,520 --> 00:19:14,760
Good.

182
00:19:16,560 --> 00:19:18,560
Serving the King isn't all you'll do.

183
00:19:18,560 --> 00:19:22,200
You must also study
the subjects that interest him.

184
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:28,560
These include literature, music,
statecraft, and warfare.

185
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:31,080
Will you teach me all of that, my lady?

186
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:37,440
You'll have to learn on your own.

187
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:44,800
Where am I supposed to learn all that?

188
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:02,880
May I ask you a favor, Your Highnesses?

189
00:20:02,880 --> 00:20:04,560
That pronoun...

190
00:20:04,560 --> 00:20:06,320
Why are you calling yourself that?

191
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:08,640
You needn't be so formal with us.

192
00:20:08,640 --> 00:20:10,360
Those were Lady Homjan's instructions.

193
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:15,680
At Wiang Kaew, I must use that pronoun
when speaking to a prince.

194
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:17,640
Just speak to us as you always have.

195
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:20,640
We're not at Wiang Kaew.

196
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:22,600
I can't, Your Highness.

197
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:27,400
If I accidentally use the wrong pronoun,

198
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:31,120
I could lose my head, Your Highness.

199
00:20:31,120 --> 00:20:36,240
Fongnuan, enough with the formalities.
You're giving me a headache.

200
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:41,200
Use whichever pronoun feels natural to you.

201
00:20:42,480 --> 00:20:46,160
Anyway, what did you need our help with?

202
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:49,960
I need to learn about His Majesty's interests.

203
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:53,400
Literature, music,

204
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:57,040
statecraft, and warfare.

205
00:20:57,040 --> 00:21:01,400
I thought you two might be able to teach me.

206
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:03,120
- Of course.
- Of course.

207
00:21:03,120 --> 00:21:04,840
That's great!

208
00:21:10,160 --> 00:21:12,960
What can each of you teach me,
Your Highnesses?

209
00:21:27,480 --> 00:21:31,040
If you'd been born 200 years later,

210
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:34,000
you could've become a music star.

211
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,440
What?

212
00:21:35,440 --> 00:21:41,360
I mean, you're talented enough
to be a professional musician.

213
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:43,880
This is the Royal Library.

214
00:21:43,880 --> 00:21:47,320
You'll find plenty of records
on governance and trade here.

215
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:49,800
They'll help you understand Ullavee better.

216
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:57,160
Then let me ask you something.
Who is Ullavee's queen now?

217
00:21:58,840 --> 00:22:02,920
After Queen Chao Oun,
Indraraja's mother, passed away,

218
00:22:02,920 --> 00:22:05,560
Father never appointed another queen.

219
00:22:05,560 --> 00:22:07,800
Well...

220
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:11,640
What about your mother and Prince Fah Haam's?

221
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:15,840
I haven't seen either of them
since I arrived in Ullavee.

222
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:21,560
Royal Consort Saeng Nguean,

223
00:22:22,760 --> 00:22:27,280
my mother, disappeared when I was young.

224
00:22:28,640 --> 00:22:33,440
Royal Consort In Kaew, Fah Haam's mother,

225
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:36,520
died shortly after he was born.

226
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:43,280
I'm sorry I asked, Your Highness.

227
00:22:43,280 --> 00:22:45,480
It's all right, Fongnuan.

228
00:22:46,800 --> 00:22:49,080
I'm ready to learn, Senior.

229
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:52,720
Jerng is more than just a martial art.

230
00:22:52,720 --> 00:22:54,640
It also requires focus.

231
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:57,840
Your mind and body must move as one.

232
00:22:57,840 --> 00:23:01,200
Your hands and feet must work together.

233
00:23:01,200 --> 00:23:03,880
Keep your stance firm and your strides steady.

234
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:05,480
Strides?

235
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:09,040
A stride is one of the basic movements
in martial arts.

236
00:23:09,040 --> 00:23:12,040
Step slowly but firmly.

237
00:23:12,040 --> 00:23:14,120
It helps you keep your balance.

238
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:18,720
If your footing is off,
your opponent will have an opening to strike.

239
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:21,520
Strum harder.

240
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:36,680
I've learned so much in just one day.
Soon I'll be better than you!

241
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:48,000
I told you to stand firm. Chest up!

242
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,600
What about trade, Your Highness?
Salt, for example.

243
00:23:50,600 --> 00:23:56,400
Sister Maneethip told me
Ullavee and Wang Nam Lin developed close ties

244
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:59,320
because Wang Nam Lin produces so much salt.

245
00:23:59,320 --> 00:24:01,520
Have I passed now?

246
00:24:02,440 --> 00:24:06,240
- Listen to this.
- There. That's the sound of my heart.

247
00:24:07,960 --> 00:24:08,840
Doesn't it sound lovely, Your Highness?

248
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:11,360
- Ullavee.
- Ullavee.

249
00:24:11,360 --> 00:24:12,560
Wang Nam Lin.

250
00:24:12,560 --> 00:24:14,600
- That's where the salt fields are.
- Yes.

251
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:17,280
The military camps...

252
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:20,040
The east. The west.

253
00:24:20,040 --> 00:24:22,920
Merng Mang. And the borders.

254
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:27,360
It sounds better the longer I listen.

255
00:24:28,800 --> 00:24:31,120
Then play it for Father.

256
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:38,880
I'm exhausted.

257
00:24:38,880 --> 00:24:41,000
You're going too fast, Senior.

258
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:43,480
- Work on your strides. Stride.
- Senior!

259
00:24:45,400 --> 00:24:47,160
Good heavens!

260
00:25:07,880 --> 00:25:09,240
Your turn.

261
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,360
Move your fingers like this.

262
00:25:36,560 --> 00:25:39,080
Why are you only teaching her
sad songs, Your Highness?

263
00:25:45,360 --> 00:25:48,880
My name is Bua Sai.
I'm the music troupe leader's daughter.

264
00:25:48,880 --> 00:25:51,960
We're performing
at the City Longevity Ceremony.

265
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:55,280
I see. I'm Fongnuan.

266
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:59,440
All these sad songs...

267
00:25:59,440 --> 00:26:04,400
I wonder if her teacher
has had his heart broken.

268
00:26:06,360 --> 00:26:08,880
I'd like to learn some cheerful songs, too.

269
00:26:08,880 --> 00:26:12,120
- Could you teach me, Bua Sai?
- No.

270
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:14,560
A student shouldn't have too many teachers.

271
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:21,640
Lady Fongnuan,
you should learn from Prince Fah Haam.

272
00:26:21,640 --> 00:26:24,680
I can teach you cheerful songs another time.

273
00:26:36,040 --> 00:26:37,280
Let's continue.

274
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:40,640
Excuse me a moment.

275
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:45,440
Hey! Prince Fah Haam!

276
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:47,880
I've only learned one note!

277
00:26:50,320 --> 00:26:54,040
Wait! My lady.

278
00:26:54,040 --> 00:26:55,400
Hold on.

279
00:26:56,600 --> 00:26:57,840
My lady.

280
00:27:00,640 --> 00:27:03,240
I haven't even told you my name.

281
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:05,880
How did you know I'm Prince Fah Haam?

282
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:09,160
I know more than just your name.

283
00:27:09,160 --> 00:27:13,520
I also know why your music sounds so sorrowful.

284
00:27:15,920 --> 00:27:18,400
You still haven't forgotten Nam Nang.

285
00:27:19,240 --> 00:27:20,920
How did you know?

286
00:27:22,240 --> 00:27:24,560
Nam Nang is a close friend of mine.

287
00:27:34,440 --> 00:27:35,920
So...

288
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:40,480
What did she say about me?

289
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:46,080
She didn't say much about you.
She told me why she was angry.

290
00:27:46,080 --> 00:27:49,080
You were a prince all along.

291
00:27:49,760 --> 00:27:52,240
You never told her the truth.

292
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:58,400
I understand how she feels,
but I see things differently.

293
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:03,320
I don't mind that you're a prince.

294
00:28:03,960 --> 00:28:06,200
But I can't stand liars.

295
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:13,800
Love built on lies
can never last, Your Highness.

296
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:23,760
Forgive me for speaking so bluntly.

297
00:28:24,480 --> 00:28:26,640
I hope you won't take offense.

298
00:28:29,360 --> 00:28:33,440
And don't think I've fallen for you.

299
00:28:34,760 --> 00:28:39,320
At least not yet.

300
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,840
Jom Harn.

301
00:29:13,280 --> 00:29:15,840
Have you heard about your father and brother?

302
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:21,560
I have.
You should be happy for Mueang Fah, Mother.

303
00:29:23,400 --> 00:29:26,080
I suspect Indraraja is plotting something.

304
00:29:27,360 --> 00:29:30,240
He's placed Mueang Fah
right by your father's side.

305
00:29:31,280 --> 00:29:35,280
He must be using your brother
to spy on everything at Wiang Kaew.

306
00:29:38,760 --> 00:29:43,120
Or perhaps Indraraja is worried
he might lose his title.

307
00:29:44,760 --> 00:29:48,720
Word has spread throughout the city
that he's been illegally collecting tribute.

308
00:29:48,720 --> 00:29:51,240
Perhaps he's using your brother

309
00:29:51,240 --> 00:29:54,920
to stop the caravan merchants
from petitioning your father.

310
00:29:55,680 --> 00:29:57,680
- Mother--
- Or perhaps...

311
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:03,000
he plans to replace Muen In with your brother?

312
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,440
Build his army? Prove his worth?

313
00:30:07,160 --> 00:30:08,560
Or could he be...

314
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:13,040
plotting to assassinate the King?

315
00:30:14,240 --> 00:30:16,080
Good heavens, Mother!

316
00:30:16,800 --> 00:30:20,960
Mueang Fah would never harm Father!

317
00:30:22,200 --> 00:30:26,760
My brother isn't so easily manipulated.

318
00:30:26,760 --> 00:30:30,520
He only sided with Indraraja
because he wanted to come home.

319
00:30:30,520 --> 00:30:32,640
He wants to return to Ullavee.

320
00:30:33,760 --> 00:30:35,840
You know that.

321
00:30:41,920 --> 00:30:44,560
Don't look at me as though it's my fault.

322
00:30:45,480 --> 00:30:48,680
Your brother was born
during the Hour of the Plunderer.

323
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:51,400
That's why he was exiled to the border
and forbidden to return to Ullavee.

324
00:30:51,400 --> 00:30:55,240
Yet Indraraja managed to change Father's mind.

325
00:30:57,040 --> 00:31:02,200
If you'd stood up for Mueang Fah back then,
he would be here with us now.

326
00:31:06,800 --> 00:31:10,160
I've never believed
in the Hour of the Plunderer.

327
00:31:10,160 --> 00:31:12,600
Mueang Fah has been back
in Ullavee for some time.

328
00:31:12,600 --> 00:31:15,080
Father hasn't shown any concern.

329
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:21,720
The only person who's troubled by it
is you, Mother.

330
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:46,800
You've finally returned to Wiang Kaew.

331
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:49,240
But...

332
00:31:50,360 --> 00:31:53,040
my stay is only temporary, Your Highness.

333
00:31:53,040 --> 00:31:55,400
I'll do everything I can
to win Father's approval,

334
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:59,320
so I can stay in Ullavee for good.

335
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:08,400
I'll determine an auspicious time
for you to enter Wiang Kaew...

336
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:10,440
without any trouble.

337
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:14,520
An auspicious time?

338
00:32:15,840 --> 00:32:17,640
The Hour of the Ruler.

339
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:23,840
It's an auspicious time to receive a new title.

340
00:32:23,840 --> 00:32:27,080
If you enter Wiang Kaew at that hour,

341
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:30,200
great fortune will await you,

342
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:34,800
along with power and honor.

343
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:42,360
Once you're in Wiang Kaew,
you must be very careful.

344
00:32:42,360 --> 00:32:47,360
Don't put yourself in danger
or those you hold dear.

345
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:51,040
I've always been careful.

346
00:33:05,040 --> 00:33:08,720
Wiang Kaew is more than the King's residence.

347
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:14,200
Everyone there must fight to survive.

348
00:33:14,200 --> 00:33:17,520
It offers great rewards,
but also great dangers.

349
00:33:17,520 --> 00:33:22,640
Your abilities alone
won't be enough to survive there.

350
00:33:22,640 --> 00:33:25,520
You'll need to use your wits.

351
00:33:26,520 --> 00:33:28,360
So think carefully.

352
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:32,920
Don't do anything reckless.

353
00:33:32,920 --> 00:33:37,080
Others could suffer
the consequences of your actions.

354
00:33:38,200 --> 00:33:42,560
Your sister, Saen Thep,

355
00:33:44,480 --> 00:33:48,440
and I could all be dragged into trouble.

356
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:51,160
Do you understand?

357
00:33:51,960 --> 00:33:53,640
Yes, Your Highness.

358
00:33:53,640 --> 00:33:57,440
Mother is right. You must be careful.

359
00:33:58,520 --> 00:34:01,280
But Lady Homjan chose you
to serve at Wiang Kaew.

360
00:34:01,280 --> 00:34:03,480
I'm sure she'll look after you.

361
00:34:04,320 --> 00:34:06,200
Can she really be trusted?

362
00:34:07,760 --> 00:34:12,000
You can't trust anyone at Wiang Kaew.

363
00:34:14,680 --> 00:34:18,320
Now hurry, or you'll be late.

364
00:34:31,120 --> 00:34:32,600
Maneethip.

365
00:34:35,760 --> 00:34:40,480
Whatever path you choose,
keep your thoughts pure,

366
00:34:40,480 --> 00:34:44,440
speak kindly, and do good deeds.

367
00:34:44,440 --> 00:34:46,560
Never wish harm upon anyone,

368
00:34:47,840 --> 00:34:50,360
and your good deeds will protect you.

369
00:34:51,400 --> 00:34:53,560
I'll remember that.

370
00:34:57,360 --> 00:35:02,240
Lha, if anything happens,

371
00:35:02,240 --> 00:35:04,600
send word to me immediately.

372
00:35:04,600 --> 00:35:06,440
I'll return at once.

373
00:35:07,160 --> 00:35:08,520
Yes, my lady.

374
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:17,960
Lady Fongnuan,
please take good care of yourself.

375
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:48,760
You may have pushed your way
into Wiang Kaew today,

376
00:35:48,760 --> 00:35:51,560
but don't think
you'll get any further than that.

377
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:57,520
I don't want to be in Wiang Kaew,
but I have no choice.

378
00:35:58,440 --> 00:36:00,880
You claim you have no choice,

379
00:36:00,880 --> 00:36:05,400
yet you chose to place yourself near my father.

380
00:36:07,360 --> 00:36:11,160
I only do what I must to survive.

381
00:36:11,160 --> 00:36:16,160
You know Ullavee is not a place where
people are free to choose how they live.

382
00:36:16,840 --> 00:36:21,520
Even you, the King's own daughter,
cannot choose your own fate.

383
00:36:21,520 --> 00:36:23,640
- What a sharp tongue!
- Go ahead, Your Highness.

384
00:36:24,640 --> 00:36:27,320
Slap me, then explain to the King...

385
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:31,840
why you struck his outer-court lady-in-waiting.

386
00:36:31,840 --> 00:36:33,560
Hit me hard.

387
00:36:33,560 --> 00:36:38,160
Better yet, leave a mark on my face,
so there's clear evidence of what happened.

388
00:36:45,040 --> 00:36:47,800
You haven't even set foot in Wiang Kaew,

389
00:36:48,640 --> 00:36:50,760
yet you're already so insolent.

390
00:36:50,760 --> 00:36:56,640
I'll wait and see how long
someone like you can survive in there.

391
00:37:00,120 --> 00:37:02,280
Do whatever you wish.

392
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:04,920
If you'll excuse me, Your Highness.

393
00:37:28,840 --> 00:37:32,640
- Junior.
- Hey, Senior.

394
00:37:32,640 --> 00:37:36,160
I was just about to visit you
at Saen Thep's residence.

395
00:37:36,160 --> 00:37:39,080
So, where are you headed?

396
00:37:42,240 --> 00:37:43,920
Wiang Kaew.

397
00:37:47,720 --> 00:37:49,240
Senior.

398
00:37:50,480 --> 00:37:52,920
What are you going to warn me about?

399
00:37:52,920 --> 00:37:56,120
I haven't even entered Wiang Kaew,
and I'm already frightened.

400
00:37:56,120 --> 00:37:59,280
Junior. Don't be afraid.

401
00:37:59,280 --> 00:38:01,560
I'm not here to warn you.

402
00:38:01,560 --> 00:38:03,280
I'm just here...

403
00:38:04,960 --> 00:38:08,640
to find someone I feel comfortable talking to.

404
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:13,680
Me?

405
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:19,200
Go ahead, then, Your Highness.

406
00:38:30,800 --> 00:38:33,320
It's about your mother and brother, isn't it?

407
00:38:36,560 --> 00:38:37,160
How did you know?

408
00:38:37,160 --> 00:38:39,680
At Maneethip's bedding ceremony,

409
00:38:39,680 --> 00:38:43,520
I noticed Prince Mueang Fah sitting
on the opposite side,

410
00:38:43,520 --> 00:38:47,640
rather than beside Royal Consort Sukantha,
like you did.

411
00:38:47,640 --> 00:38:50,360
And ever since Prince Mueang Fah returned
to Ullavee,

412
00:38:50,360 --> 00:38:52,560
he has spent his nights at Wat Singhasna

413
00:38:52,560 --> 00:38:55,560
instead of
at Royal Consort Sukantha's residence.

414
00:38:55,560 --> 00:38:58,400
And I once saw...

415
00:38:58,400 --> 00:39:02,920
Prince Mueang Fah rowing a boat alone
and picking lotus flowers at Wat Singhasna.

416
00:39:02,920 --> 00:39:06,040
- He looked terribly lonely, Your Highness.
- Nosy.

417
00:39:06,040 --> 00:39:10,120
- And you're quite the nosy one yourself.
- Senior!

418
00:39:10,120 --> 00:39:13,360
You'd better call it being observant.

419
00:39:13,360 --> 00:39:17,600
I need to learn these things
if I'm going to survive here.

420
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:23,120
Are you afraid of Mueang Fah, too,
like everyone else?

421
00:39:25,840 --> 00:39:29,960
I have my own reasons for being afraid of him.

422
00:39:31,040 --> 00:39:34,960
So why is everyone else afraid of him?

423
00:39:40,240 --> 00:39:44,400
Have you ever heard
of the "Hour of the Plunderer"?

424
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:54,960
It is the hour in which a destroyer is born,

425
00:39:54,960 --> 00:39:57,560
one believed to bring calamity upon the realm.

426
00:39:58,880 --> 00:40:00,720
Mueang Fah...

427
00:40:02,640 --> 00:40:04,640
was born in the Hour of the Plunderer.

428
00:40:06,080 --> 00:40:09,000
That is why he was exiled to the border
at a young age.

429
00:40:10,720 --> 00:40:12,800
Mother cannot let go of the belief...

430
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:17,640
that Mueang Fah is the reason
she never became Queen.

431
00:40:24,200 --> 00:40:26,320
I felt sorry for him,

432
00:40:27,240 --> 00:40:33,080
but back then I was too young
to do anything to help.

433
00:40:36,360 --> 00:40:37,880
Senior.

434
00:40:39,560 --> 00:40:42,480
You're such a kind person.

435
00:40:43,720 --> 00:40:47,520
You worry so much about others
that you feel unhappy.

436
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:53,280
But being unhappy won't solve anything.

437
00:40:55,360 --> 00:40:59,840
Some things are just beyond our control.

438
00:41:00,920 --> 00:41:03,040
If you ask me,

439
00:41:03,720 --> 00:41:08,560
the only thing you can do
is take good care of yourself.

440
00:41:09,680 --> 00:41:14,160
Because you'll be looking after those two
for a long time to come.

441
00:41:16,480 --> 00:41:20,960
Neither of them is likely to back down.

442
00:41:22,920 --> 00:41:28,640
Someone who can't swim shouldn't try
to save someone who's drowning.

443
00:41:35,320 --> 00:41:36,800
Well said!

444
00:41:39,320 --> 00:41:43,480
Junior, you really know how to cheer me up.

445
00:41:44,360 --> 00:41:50,280
Now, I hope you'll stay safe in Wiang Kaew.

446
00:41:51,560 --> 00:41:54,720
Mueang Fah is also making his way
to Wiang Kaew.

447
00:41:54,720 --> 00:41:57,960
I'll ask him to look after you.

448
00:41:57,960 --> 00:42:02,160
No, Your Highness.
I don't need anyone looking after me.

449
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:05,360
I can take care of myself.

450
00:42:09,120 --> 00:42:14,120
If you really want to help me,
then help me with something else.

451
00:42:15,080 --> 00:42:16,440
What is it?

452
00:42:30,320 --> 00:42:33,080
This room has been specially prepared for you.

453
00:42:33,080 --> 00:42:37,400
You may rest here at ease.

454
00:42:43,560 --> 00:42:49,520
Has the new lady-in-waiting whom Homjan
assigned to serve Father arrived yet?

455
00:42:50,800 --> 00:42:51,880
Yes, Your Highness.

456
00:42:53,600 --> 00:42:55,920
Today is her first day as well.

457
00:43:24,960 --> 00:43:27,600
This is your accommodation.

458
00:43:27,600 --> 00:43:32,760
You'll be staying here from now on.
You must learn to adjust.

459
00:43:32,760 --> 00:43:34,280
Yes, my lady.

460
00:43:34,280 --> 00:43:36,520
Tidy your belongings.

461
00:43:37,400 --> 00:43:40,440
You shall present yourself
before the King tomorrow.

462
00:43:40,440 --> 00:43:42,520
Tomorrow already?

463
00:43:42,520 --> 00:43:44,240
Yes.

464
00:43:44,240 --> 00:43:46,160
Be prepared.

465
00:44:02,480 --> 00:44:07,360
Dao Kaew has returned from Wang Nam Lin
with the information you wish to find.

466
00:44:07,360 --> 00:44:09,160
What did she find out?

467
00:44:10,840 --> 00:44:13,640
Let me ask you once more.

468
00:44:14,440 --> 00:44:20,080
Are you still determined to learn about
Princess Maneethip's past, Your Highness?

469
00:44:33,440 --> 00:44:35,320
I'm prepared to hear it all.

470
00:44:37,320 --> 00:44:39,160
Tell me everything.

471
00:44:41,880 --> 00:44:47,680
Princess Maneethip did have a lover,
just as you suspected.

472
00:44:57,440 --> 00:45:02,920
She and General In Saeng
had been close since childhood.

473
00:45:03,720 --> 00:45:09,600
He served as her royal guard
and taught her everything.

474
00:45:09,600 --> 00:45:14,160
He was also the person she trusted most.

475
00:45:15,720 --> 00:45:18,040
As they grew older,

476
00:45:18,040 --> 00:45:23,640
their bond grew into love.

477
00:45:25,040 --> 00:45:29,160
Once the royal proposal
for Princess Maneethip was sent,

478
00:45:30,480 --> 00:45:34,160
General In Saeng was sent away to the border,

479
00:45:34,760 --> 00:45:40,200
so he wouldn't stand
between you and the princess.

480
00:46:08,160 --> 00:46:10,240
<i>Do not grieve, my princess.</i>

481
00:46:12,640 --> 00:46:14,440
<i>I understand.</i>

482
00:46:15,480 --> 00:46:19,880
<i>We both have duties to fulfill for our realm.</i>

483
00:46:25,640 --> 00:46:31,480
<i>In this life,
fate may not allow us to be together,</i>

484
00:46:33,280 --> 00:46:34,880
<i>but this love...</i>

485
00:46:36,840 --> 00:46:39,280
<i>shall remain in my heart...</i>

486
00:46:41,760 --> 00:46:43,280
<i>forever.</i>

487
00:47:00,640 --> 00:47:02,440
<i>These orchids...</i>

488
00:47:04,520 --> 00:47:06,840
<i>will bloom in my heart...</i>

489
00:47:11,360 --> 00:47:13,880
<i>until my dying breath.</i>

490
00:48:12,640 --> 00:48:13,880
<i>Hyah!</i>

491
00:48:21,320 --> 00:48:22,600
<i>Hyah!</i>

492
00:48:49,520 --> 00:48:51,760
I never knew any of this.

493
00:48:52,880 --> 00:48:54,600
Had I known,

494
00:48:55,640 --> 00:48:59,760
I would never have asked Father
to send a royal proposal for her hand.

495
00:48:59,760 --> 00:49:03,360
No outsiders knew, Your Highness.

496
00:49:03,360 --> 00:49:05,800
The King of Wang Nam Lin...

497
00:49:06,680 --> 00:49:10,600
ordered that the matter be kept secret.

498
00:49:14,360 --> 00:49:16,080
So now,

499
00:49:18,080 --> 00:49:20,280
what became of General In Saeng?

500
00:49:42,920 --> 00:49:45,840
Your Highness! Your Highness!

501
00:49:47,040 --> 00:49:49,600
Why did you rush in like that?
What is it, Lha?

502
00:49:51,360 --> 00:49:55,560
A messenger from Wang Nam Lin has arrived
with news from the soldiers.

503
00:49:57,360 --> 00:49:58,960
What news?

504
00:50:03,360 --> 00:50:05,120
What's in that pouch, Lha?

505
00:50:09,840 --> 00:50:11,200
Lha.

506
00:50:41,440 --> 00:50:43,200
Lha, what is the news?

507
00:50:48,040 --> 00:50:49,840
What happened to In Saeng?

508
00:50:54,680 --> 00:50:56,680
Lha, tell me at once!

509
00:51:02,640 --> 00:51:04,680
General In Saeng...

510
00:51:06,400 --> 00:51:10,640
died two days ago from jungle fever
while stationed at the border.

511
00:51:19,000 --> 00:51:24,040
This news should reach Princess Maneethip soon.

512
00:51:53,360 --> 00:51:55,520
With his dying breath,

513
00:51:57,320 --> 00:51:59,440
General In Saeng asked his men

514
00:51:59,440 --> 00:52:02,200
to deliver this head cloth
to you, Princess Maneethip.

515
00:52:29,320 --> 00:52:30,840
This is all because of me.

516
00:52:33,720 --> 00:52:36,200
If I hadn't taken Maneethip away from him,

517
00:52:40,440 --> 00:52:43,720
General In Saeng would
never have been sent to the border...

518
00:52:48,480 --> 00:52:50,440
and he wouldn't have died this way.

519
00:52:52,440 --> 00:52:57,560
Humans cannot defy the fate decreed by Heaven.

520
00:52:58,640 --> 00:53:03,600
Whether it be love...

521
00:53:04,920 --> 00:53:07,000
or death.

522
00:53:32,640 --> 00:53:34,280
Why?

523
00:53:40,360 --> 00:53:42,160
<i>In this life,</i>

524
00:53:43,040 --> 00:53:46,240
<i>fate may not allow us to be together,</i>

525
00:53:47,280 --> 00:53:48,840
<i>but this love...</i>

526
00:53:50,800 --> 00:53:53,280
<i>shall remain in my heart...</i>

527
00:53:55,680 --> 00:53:57,280
<i>forever.</i>

528
00:54:05,960 --> 00:54:07,680
Why couldn't it have been me who died instead?

529
00:54:07,680 --> 00:54:10,880
Princess Maneethip, please don't do this!

530
00:54:12,480 --> 00:54:14,800
Please don't. Your Highness.

531
00:54:21,880 --> 00:54:24,040
Because of me...

532
00:54:28,240 --> 00:54:33,040
In Saeng died because of me.

533
00:54:37,280 --> 00:54:39,640
I'd like to tell you.

534
00:54:41,280 --> 00:54:43,480
I didn't come here...

535
00:54:45,440 --> 00:54:49,880
out of ambition or greed.

536
00:54:51,440 --> 00:54:56,320
I know that if I disobey the royal decree,

537
00:54:56,320 --> 00:54:59,160
those around me will suffer the consequences.

538
00:55:00,160 --> 00:55:02,040
I don't want my sister...

539
00:55:02,040 --> 00:55:05,160
or Prince Saen Thep
to get dragged into trouble because of me.

540
00:55:06,080 --> 00:55:08,800
I will do my best to fulfill my duties.

541
00:55:08,800 --> 00:55:13,280
And if I ever make a mistake, please punish me.

542
00:55:14,600 --> 00:55:17,960
Don't let others suffer for my mistakes.

543
00:55:17,960 --> 00:55:23,280
I have no desire for grand titles
or special privileges.

544
00:55:24,800 --> 00:55:27,880
I simply want to perform my duties
to the best of my ability...

545
00:55:29,000 --> 00:55:32,040
and make it through each day safely.

546
00:55:41,040 --> 00:55:44,200
Don't you think you're asking for too little?

547
00:55:44,200 --> 00:55:49,440
Being too ambitious will only bring trouble.

548
00:55:51,080 --> 00:55:54,800
No human plan can defy the will of Heaven.

549
00:55:54,800 --> 00:55:58,720
Sometimes, you may be forced
to accept things you never wanted.

550
00:55:58,720 --> 00:56:00,960
Leave that for the future.

551
00:56:00,960 --> 00:56:05,440
There's no use worrying
about things that haven't happened yet.

552
00:56:06,080 --> 00:56:10,200
I will respect your wishes.

553
00:56:10,200 --> 00:56:14,320
But my wishes, you must follow.

554
00:56:14,320 --> 00:56:17,440
Now, tidy your belongings and get ready.

555
00:56:17,440 --> 00:56:20,360
We must present ourselves
before the King tomorrow.

556
00:56:20,360 --> 00:56:21,600
Yes, my lady.

557
00:57:31,120 --> 00:57:33,000
[Next Episode]
<i>What you must help me with,</i>

558
00:57:33,000 --> 00:57:36,320
<i>besides hand-rolling tobacco, is serving tea.</i>

559
00:57:36,320 --> 00:57:39,640
<i>Lady Homjan and Fongnuan are here
to serve you, Your Majesty.</i>

560
00:57:39,640 --> 00:57:43,960
<i>If I accidentally hurt the King,
will I be executed?</i>

561
00:57:43,960 --> 00:57:47,480
<i>Why must I keep an eye on Fongnuan?
She's merely a lady-in-waiting.</i>

562
00:57:47,480 --> 00:57:49,040
<i>She hardly seems like a threat.</i>

563
00:57:49,040 --> 00:57:50,600
<i>Given the circumstances,</i>

564
00:57:50,600 --> 00:57:54,360
<i>you should know what you ought
and ought not to do.</i>

565
00:57:54,360 --> 00:57:57,360
<i>If I had to choose
between falling in love and catching bandits,</i>

566
00:57:57,360 --> 00:57:59,000
<i>I'd much rather go after bandits.</i>

567
00:57:59,000 --> 00:58:02,560
<i>I thank you on Maneethip's behalf.</i>

568
00:58:02,560 --> 00:58:06,320
<i>I shall devote myself to caring for Maneethip
to the best of my ability.</i>
